1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,749
A memecoin you light together.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:09,140
A first-time visitor: no wallet, no sign-up.

3
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:12,527
One tap brings two hundred EMBER of free kindling.

4
00:00:12,577 --> 00:00:18,974
The pile is cold, so wood counts almost four
times. Throw a hundred: the firestarter.

5
00:00:19,668 --> 00:00:25,600
Then the demo bots, each labelled as a bot.
Two early ones share your quarter of the night.

6
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:29,803
A steady one follows. The pile climbs toward the line.

7
00:00:29,853 --> 00:00:35,076
A sniper waits for the end, then
closes the gap: the last log.

8
00:00:35,276 --> 00:00:40,763
Dawn: the fire caught. Everyone gets
their wood back, plus new EMBER.

9
00:00:40,813 --> 00:00:47,928
Early wood earns most: the same
100 got 4.26 early, 1.08 sniped.

10
00:00:48,128 --> 00:00:51,931
Next night the bots and the visitor hold back, on purpose.

11
00:00:51,981 --> 00:00:57,239
Too little wood: the fire smokes,
and three percent of the pile burns.

12
00:00:58,814 --> 00:01:03,669
Three lit nights later, the coin's face reads LIT ×3.

13
00:01:03,719 --> 00:01:08,177
The contract draws it, so every
wallet shows tonight's fire.

14
00:01:08,377 --> 00:01:15,425
Every tap was a real transaction. And the
contract has no keys: nobody can change a rule.

15
00:01:15,625 --> 00:01:18,870
Sixty simulated nights picked every number.

16
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:25,543
Bonfire. Play it on NEAR testnet, no wallet needed.

17
00:01:25,593 --> 00:01:28,836
Would you throw early, or wait and snipe?

